        "subject": "Console: WhatsApp verification Required or Deferred for testing, test staff, the deferral's lifecycle and the pilot mark (D224)",
        "body": "Console: WhatsApp verification Required or Deferred for testing, test staff, the deferral's lifecycle and the pilot mark (D224)\n\n- Create a business: for a test business, while the server says deferral is\n  available (platform/capabilities), a \"WhatsApp verification\" field —\n  \"Required before activation\" by default, or \"Deferred for testing\" with a\n  written reason, the controlled-test confirmation, an optional review date and\n  the warning, word for word. A deferred Owner's setup code is shown once.\n- A test business's page:\n  - Add test staff (Manager or Employee, a unique number, optional email, stores,\n    the verification policy), each with their own setup code shown once;\n  - Deferred accounts: who granted the exception, when and why, the review\n    date and the setup code's state; require verification (nothing is sent),\n    edit the reason or date, reissue or revoke the code, cancel the account.\n    There is no way to mark anyone verified;\n  - the store-pilot mark.\n- A deferred number reads \"Deferred — not verified\" everywhere, never \"verified\";\n  the businesses list filters to businesses with deferred verification.\n- EN/FR/AR. In Arabic the pilot is a \"field run\" (تشغيل ميداني): the catalogue\n  keeps تجريبي for the free trial.\n- Tests: deferred-verification-console (12); the shared fixture answers the two\n  new reads (deferral off, none deferred).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
        "author": {
          "name": "CLAUDE",
          "email": "abdelkerim.mahfoudh@gmail.com",
          "time": 1793219518000
